    "progressSummary": "PROGRESS: matrix/SL₂(ℤ) form of Bézout proved (bezout-identity-oq-01-oq-02), 0-axiom, verified",
    "builtItems": [
      "eStep, eStep_det, eStep_apply, eStep_euclid in Proofs/BezoutIdentityOQ01OQ02.lean (elementary step matrix, det -1, one Euclidean round)",
      "det_mul_unimodular, mulVec_two (unimodular closure under multiplication; 2×2 matrix action on a length-2 column)",
      "bezoutMatrix, gcd_cast_ne_zero, bezoutMatrix_det, bezoutMatrix_mulVec (Bézout matrix in SL₂(ℤ), reduces (a,b)ᵀ to (g,0)ᵀ)",
      "bezoutSL, bezout_unimodular_reduction (main theorem: matrix form of Bézout via Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℤ). 9 thm, 3 def, 175 lines, 0 axioms."
    ],
    "insights": [
      "The extended Euclidean algorithm IS an SL₂(ℤ) row-reduction: elementary step matrices eStep q = !![0,1;1,-q] (det -1) realise (a,b)↦(b, a%b), and their product is the Bézout coefficient matrix.",
      "The Bézout matrix !![gcdA,gcdB;-b/g,a/g] (g=gcd a b) has determinant exactly 1 (SL₂(ℤ)) and carries (a,b)ᵀ to (gcd a b, 0)ᵀ; Bézout coefficients are literally its top row.",
      "det=1 (not just ±1) is forced: g·det = a·gcdA+b·gcdB = g via Int.gcd_eq_gcd_ab, then cancel nonzero g.",
      "Proof is fully algebraic (no induction on the algorithm, no native_decide): clear exact divisions g∣a, g∣b with Int.ediv_mul_cancel and cancel g with mul_left_cancel₀; first component closed by linear_combination against Int.gcd_eq_gcd_ab."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Prove bezoutMatrix a b is literally the product of the elementary matrices eStep qᵢ for successive quotients qᵢ (reconstruct the accumulated product, not just its endpoint).",
      "Generalise to a Euclidean domain (e.g. k[X]): analogous unimodular 2×2 matrix reducing (a,b) to (gcd a b, 0)."
    ],
